---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import ServiceLinks from '../components/ServiceLinks.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
import { graph } from '../lib/patterns.js';
const ask = `mailto:${site.email}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('AI pilot for our engineering team')}`;
const bodyBg = graph({ parity: 0, seed: 12, cx: 1200, cy: 450, satellites: 80 });
---
<Base title="AI adoption for engineering teams" description="A four-week pilot that gets an engineering team real throughput from AI tooling: workflow audit, agents on one real repo, measured before and after.">
  <Hero variant="graph" seed={11} eyebrow="Service · Engineering teams" title="AI adoption for engineering teams">
    <p class="lede"><em>"We bought the AI seats and nothing changed."</em> Most teams get Copilot or Claude licenses and a Slack thread of tips. Throughput stays flat because nobody changed the workflow. I did this for a team on a production fintech platform and ticket throughput rose 65%.</p>
    <p><a class="btn btn-primary" href={ask}>Ask about a pilot</a></p>
  </Hero>

  <section class="section band-parallax">
    <div class="band-bg" data-parallax="0.55" set:html={bodyBg} aria-hidden="true" />
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>What you get: a four-week pilot</h2>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><strong>Week 1.</strong> I sit in your workflow: repo, tickets, review process, CI. I write down where the time actually goes.</li>
        <li><strong>Weeks 2–3.</strong> Agents and tooling set up on one real repo, with your engineers, on real tickets. Conventions written down so it survives me leaving.</li>
        <li><strong>Week 4.</strong> Before-and-after numbers from your own tracker, and a short list of what to do next.</li>
      </ol>
      <h2>Good fit if</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>You have a team of three to thirty engineers and a backlog that isn't shrinking.</li>
        <li>You've already paid for AI tools and can't point to what changed.</li>
        <li>You want the numbers from your own tracker, not a vendor's slide.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><span class="tag">Fixed scope</span> <span class="tag">Four weeks</span> <span class="tag">Quote on scope</span></p>
      <p><a class="btn btn-primary" href={ask}>Ask about a pilot</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ServiceLinks current="/ai-adoption" />
</Base>
